  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(\\theta\\) is a constant such that \\(0\\lt\\theta\\lt\\pi\\) and \\(x+\\frac1x=2\\cos\\theta,\\) then for each positive integer \\(n,\\) \\(x^n+\\frac1{x^n}\\) equals",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(2\\cos\\theta\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2^n\\cos\\theta\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2\\cos^n\\theta\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2\\cos n\\theta\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(2^n\\cos^n\\theta\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1981-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The equation is \\(x^2-2x\\cos\\theta+1=0,\\) whose roots are \\(e^{i\\theta}\\) and \\(e^{-i\\theta}.\\) Thus \\(x=e^{\\pm i\\theta}\\) and \\(x^{-1}=e^{\\mp i\\theta}.\\) By De Moivre’s theorem, \\[ \\begin{aligned} x^n+x^{-n} &=e^{in\\theta}+e^{-in\\theta}\\\\ &=2\\cos n\\theta. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite the condition as a quadratic equation in \\(x\\)",
        "Its two roots are \\(\\cos\\theta\\pm i\\sin\\theta\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
